gc.futterfolge.enabled.body:
Hungry tamed animals of the same kind queue up, by level and then by stars. Young animals are a kind of their own; fed animals and animals in combat or under a rider don't queue. In turn each animal takes one piece of the nearest food it can reach. An animal lets higher-ranked ones eat first for at most {gc_futterfolge_wait}, then it eats anyway.

- Pregnant ones last: {gc_futterfolge_pregnant}
- Wild animals being tamed spot food just as far, without an order: {gc_futterfolge_wild}
- Animals on a leash or at a post only count for food they can reach there.

Currently {gc_futterfolge_enabled}. Off: as in Valheim.
